---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About ScreenshotChecker — Privacy-First Visual Intelligence"
  description="Learn about ScreenshotChecker's mission, privacy-first client-side architecture, and commitment to evidence-based image investigation."
>
  <Header currentPath="/about" />

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-20">
    <!-- Hero / Title -->
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-14">
      <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold text-primary font-mono block mb-2">Our Mission</span>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-normal text-ink tracking-tight mb-5">
        Image Intelligence Built on Privacy & Evidence
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-body leading-relaxed">
        We believe that understanding, verifying, and protecting screenshots should be effortless, fast, and completely confidential.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Philosophy Cards -->
    <div class="space-y-12 text-body">
      <!-- 1. The Core Problem -->
      <section class="feature-card !p-8 space-y-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink font-normal">
          Why Screenshots Require Special Understanding
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          Screenshots are the primary currency of digital communication today: banking transaction receipts, WhatsApp messages, order confirmations, security alerts, and invoices. Yet visual evidence is easily manipulated, faked, or misunderstood.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          Traditional image tools treat every graphic as a generic bundle of pixels. ScreenshotChecker was built to behave like a visual investigator: observing context, extracting structured numbers and claims, auditing internal consistency, and warning users about social-engineering threats.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. The 3 Core Pillars -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-xl p-6 space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-surface-cream-strong flex items-center justify-center text-primary font-bold">
            1
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink font-normal">100% Client-Side</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Your images and personal data never leave your computer. OCR, metadata stripping, ELA forensics, and semantic analysis run directly inside your browser.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-xl p-6 space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-surface-cream-strong flex items-center justify-center text-primary font-bold">
            2
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink font-normal">No Fake AI Claims</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            We never return arbitrary percentage scores. If something cannot be proven from a screenshot alone (such as bank settlement), we state it clearly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-xl p-6 space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-surface-cream-strong flex items-center justify-center text-primary font-bold">
            3
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink font-normal">Connected Toolkit</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Every tool has a specialized workspace, yet all tools work together: find PII in an analysis, and immediately redact it in the editor.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. Our Technical Boundaries -->
      <section class="bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink font-normal">Our Stance on Authenticity</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-ink">Content is not authenticity.</strong> A visual receipt can be internally consistent, beautifully rendered, and completely fabricated by a mock generation app. Therefore, we explicitly distinguish <em>"looks consistent"</em> from <em>"is verified"</em> and encourage users to verify financial transactions directly through official bank portals.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
